From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: add QCA4B DSA VP offload

Allocate persistent PPE virtual ports for QCA4B-tagged QCA8386 DSA user
ports. Program and verify the ATH header ingress and egress mappings as a
transaction, use the VP in flow rules, and restore the switch state when a
port is unregistered.

Reinject VP exception traffic through the DSA conduit and expose the live
manager state plus per-VP packet counters in debugfs. Keep the generic
tag_8021q path unchanged. Release an egress VP acquired before the
flowtable lock when setup fails through the pre-lock cleanup path.

Keep QCA/QCA4B metadata RX consistent with the software tagger: packets
sent only to the CPU still require Linux bridge flooding, so do not set
the default hardware-forwarded mark on header-stripped exception frames.

Include the earlier QCA 802.1Q conduit acceptance and standalone VID
selection at this DSA port extension. Preserve the final protocol
dispatch and subsequent lifecycle changes without an extra layer.
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
